  "input": {
    "rationale": "Final source-only addition in the remaining seconds: an observation that connects two of the recorded findings and is not yet stated on its own. In both the explicit-transfer case and the growth case the operation reports success because its future is resolved by an internal event (the configuration entry committing, or the transfer goroutine taking its lost-leadership branch) that does not encode the caller's actual goal, so a successful future coexists with a lost capability. Anchors are ones already read and cited.",
    "sources": [],
    "investigations": [],
    "knowledge": [
      {
        "id": null,
        "ref": "@futures-encode-internal-events-not-caller-goals",
        "kind": "behavior",
        "statement": "The futures of the two membership/authority APIs resolve on internal events rather than on the caller's goal. A configuration-change future (AddVoter, AddNonvoter, RemoveServer, DemoteVoter) is resolved when the configuration entry commits, which in the documented growth step happens before the consequence of the change is visible, and the leadership-transfer future is resolved by the transfer goroutine's branches, including the branch that reports a lost leadership during transfer as a successful outcome. In both cases a successful future can therefore coexist with the loss of the capability the caller asked for, and the caller has no error to act on.",
        "conditions": "Protocol version 3, a leader applied to a configuration change whose consequences depend on a server that is not yet serving (witnessed in the growth receipts), and an explicit leadership transfer whose target cannot be elected (witnessed in the transfer receipts).",
