        "summary": "Allocation exhausted (about fifteen seconds left); no closing submission is needed and the retained draft stands unchanged. Recorded outcome of the run: three explained investigations, each witnessed by two independent clean-copy executions - (1) explicit leadership transfer accepts a caller-named non-voter and reports success while the named target never leads and the incumbent must re-elect; (2) one allowed StoreLogs error in the conflict-truncation window wedges a follower permanently, costs exactly one unit of commitment-quorum margin, and is repaired only by a restart or a leader snapshot install, with a stale certificate unable to win an election; (3) the documented growth sequence commits the change and returns success while removing the sole node's leadership and write availability, with no in-process API repair and the staged AddNonvoter form staying safe - with boundaries, counterevidence, limitations, scoping results and the source-level facts all recorded against their receipts."
